{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00335","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00335@rel:R25-11#73a08245","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00335","release":"R25-11","content":"function RecoverAllFiles [SWS_PER_00335] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_PER_00009 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00137 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; RecoverAllFiles (const ara::core::Instance Specifier &amp;fs) noexcept; Recovers a File Storage, including all files. RecoverAllFiles recovers a File Storage when the redundancy checks fail. It will fail with kResourceBusy when the File Storage is currently open, or when it is modified by a call from another thread to UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, ResetPersistency, RecoverAllFiles, or ResetAllFiles. This method does a best-effort recovery of all files. After recovery, files might show outdated or initial content, or might be lost. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope namespace ara::per class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kStorageNot rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fs td The shortName path of a PortPrototype typed by a PersistencyFile StorageInterface. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td Found td Returned if the passed InstanceSpecifier does not match any PersistencyFileStorageInterface configured for this Executable. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, or Reset Persistency is currently being executed, or if ResetAllFiles is currently being executed for the same File Storage, or a Shared Handle of the same File Storage is currently in use. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the recovered files. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the recovered files would exceed the configured maximumAllowedSize of the File Storage. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00335","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"RecoverAllFiles","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"namespaces/ns_per_ara_per_d9a3e9.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-90dbf15c08d6f936","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":87,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"RecoverAllFiles API in Persistency","n":9,"cap":"Figure 9.35: Interfaces for file storage","sha":"90dbf15c08d6f936c170554e8c7a2f77567241569f8f890405bc3996341e9929","nser":5,"src":"figure"}],"snippets":[{"id":"SNIP_per_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_P_P115_333","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Persistency","p":115,"rel":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"EXPLICIT_REF